# How to cite this software (GitHub's "Cite this repository"; read by Zenodo at a release). The paper's
# citation (preferred-citation) will be added when it is published.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ASTRID: Astrocyte-informed demixing of calcium imaging signals"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT    # except the folder reproduce/tuncat_eval/, which is GPL-2.0-only (see README.md)
repository-code: "https://github.com/jameschengpeng/ASTRID"
keywords:
  - calcium imaging
  - demixing
  - astrocytes
  - neuropil
  - two-photon
  - one-photon
abstract: >-
  ASTRID (ASTRocyte-Informed Demixing) demixes the calcium traces of neuronal ROIs in imaging where neurons
  and astrocytes share one fluorescence channel. For each ROI, it fits a model of the patch of pixels around
  it, with the neuron's own signal, the neighboring neurons, astrocyte components placed on astrocyte
  territory, and the local neuropil.
